EXPERIMENT-3-IMPLEMENT QUEUE USING STACKS.(LEET CODE-232)

Aim:
To implement a Queue (FIFO - First In, First Out) using two stacks and perform the operations push, pop, peek, and empty.

Algorithm
1.Create two stacks: st (main stack) and helper (temporary stack).
2.Push Operation:
  --Push the new element into st.
3.Pop Operation:
  --Move all elements from st to helper.
  --Remove and store the top element of helper (front of the queue).
  --Move the remaining elements back to st.
  --Return the removed element.
4.Peek Operation:
  --Move all elements from st to helper.
  --Read the top element of helper without removing it.
  --Move all elements back to st.
  --Return the front element.
5.Empty Operation:
  --If st is empty, return true; otherwise, return false.

CODE:
class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> st;
    stack<int> helper;

    MyQueue() {
    }

    void push(int x) {
        st.push(x);
    }

    int pop() {
        while (st.size() > 0) {
            helper.push(st.top());
            st.pop();
        }

        int x = helper.top();
        helper.pop();

        while (helper.size() > 0) {
            st.push(helper.top());
            helper.pop();
        }

        return x;
    }

    int peek() {
        while (st.size() > 0) {
            helper.push(st.top());
            st.pop();
        }

        int x = helper.top();

        while (helper.size() > 0) {
            st.push(helper.top());
            helper.pop();
        }

        return x;
    }

    bool empty() {
        if (st.size() == 0)
            return true;
        else
            return false;
    }
};
